 where i'm going to play  loud right now i don't have fast in me i  don't have dynamic in me i'm going to  really take this energy down even if  it's like the beginning of the brahms  concerto you know slow it down take your  time  and then at some point you've identified  with that low energy and you're like  okay i'm sick of it let's go  and then then it picks up and you've  completely gone through  your own evolution  with the audience  and you arrived honestly at a different  mood and everyone has been there with  you and  that i think is what is motivating  music is this channel for you rather  than  this despite  this i have to do that  if you can work with it it's amazing and  it's that thing like whatever you're  going through  there's someone out there who hears it  and feels it and needs that so the more  you can just be true to yourself  obviously not  you know  you're working with colleagues you want  to find a way to connect with your  colleagues  and  do that same emotional honesty while  playing i think that it is really a very  very special conversation at that point  you could do that in practice too you  know just take a moment and where am i  emotionally  why why do i feel this resistance what  is going on and don't fix it just like  be with that just notice it's that that  idea of notice what's going on  and just say okay name it notice it name  it leave it alone just do your thing  and i think it it's  yeah then it's not a matter of  motivation it's a matter of like living  through it  i think we have to discuss that you're  so patient  now you can stand up now i understand  what's happening if you want to stand up  you can stand up  hi um  i was just wondering for those like  students who might not necessarily be  pursuing a professional career like  playing music how can we still keep like  music like a daily part of our time  um this may be my  own inclination but i think  we can all make the world  better  by connecting  and  connecting with